                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.51/1833: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-09-24T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 24,
                                1927—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>148. Your 252, September 22, 9 a.m. No new proposals for Nicaraguan financing
                    have been brought to the Department’s attention since you were in Washington.
                    You will be kept informed by telegraph of any important developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
